1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:29,980
To be continued...

2
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,560
I betcha we can bring in a thousand people for the next show!

3
00:00:33,720 --> 00:00:36,320
If we start getting cocky, then we're sure to make a mistake.

4
00:00:36,480 --> 00:00:37,440
We should focus.

5
00:00:37,980 --> 00:00:39,320
Work calmly and steadily.

6
00:00:39,780 --> 00:00:40,120
Cool!

7
00:00:40,420 --> 00:00:43,060
So I say we do that nerdy crap Junko just said,

8
00:00:43,420 --> 00:00:44,740
and bring in that thousand!

9
00:00:45,220 --> 00:00:45,660
Yeah!

10
00:00:48,040 --> 00:00:49,700
If the movies have taught me anything,

11
00:00:49,820 --> 00:00:53,220
it's that zombies with big fat heads are way easier to kill!

12
00:00:54,640 --> 00:00:57,920
Look, if you brain-rotted suckers keep on riding the high from Arpino,

13
00:00:58,120 --> 00:00:58,920
then it's BOOM!

14
00:00:59,120 --> 00:00:59,640
Headshot!

15
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:02,980
Next show will be at Ekimai Furosan Stadium!

16
00:01:03,400 --> 00:01:04,840
EFS if you're nasty!

17
00:01:06,380 --> 00:01:07,720
Wait, I'm confused.

18
00:01:08,080 --> 00:01:08,980
Where'd you say again?

19
00:01:09,820 --> 00:01:10,580
What's wrong?

20
00:01:10,980 --> 00:01:13,660
Yeah, I don't think I've ever heard of that venue before.

21
00:01:14,080 --> 00:01:16,360
Eh, not like I care where they call the place.

22
00:01:16,560 --> 00:01:19,480
Point is, we're putting a thousand butts in the seats this time.

23
00:01:19,880 --> 00:01:20,360
Actually,

24
00:01:21,220 --> 00:01:23,400
the name won't be changed until February.

25
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:26,000
I see somebody's done their homework.

26
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:28,020
Oh, no wonder it doesn't ring a bell.

27
00:01:28,760 --> 00:01:29,960
So what's it called now?

28
00:01:29,960 --> 00:01:32,800
The best amenity stadium.

29
00:01:32,800 --> 00:01:35,600
The huge one in Tosu.

30
00:01:35,600 --> 00:01:40,440
Uh, isn't that...

31
00:01:40,440 --> 00:01:42,220
I promise I'll be okay.

32
00:01:42,220 --> 00:01:45,160
The biggest issue is the size of the place.

33
00:01:45,160 --> 00:01:48,560
I think the capacity is around...

34
00:01:48,560 --> 00:01:49,560
25,000.

35
00:01:49,560 --> 00:01:50,220
25,000?

36
00:01:50,220 --> 00:01:51,400
That's like 50 Arpinos!

37
00:01:51,400 --> 00:01:57,980
And with the field, there's standing room for even more.

38
00:01:58,700 --> 00:02:02,000
If this thing goes south, could I take out that many people?

39
00:02:02,380 --> 00:02:03,600
This is a really big deal.

40
00:02:03,600 --> 00:02:05,100
There's no way we'll pull it off!

41
00:02:05,100 --> 00:02:09,060
The concert is scheduled for March 8th.

42
00:02:09,060 --> 00:02:09,920
Don't be an idiot!

43
00:02:10,460 --> 00:02:12,420
A whole stadium here in Saga?

44
00:02:12,800 --> 00:02:14,140
We could never fill it up!

45
00:02:14,620 --> 00:02:15,900
Iron Frill did it back then, but...

46
00:02:15,900 --> 00:02:18,420
So that was them then, and this is you now!

47
00:02:20,420 --> 00:02:21,600
Oh, I'm sorry.

48
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:25,900
Do you knuckleheads honestly believe Iron Frill was better 10 years ago than you are today?

49
00:02:25,960 --> 00:02:27,220
Because that is idiotic!

50
00:02:28,220 --> 00:02:31,240
Your legends, each and every...

51
00:02:31,240 --> 00:02:37,300
All except one of you, that is.

52
00:02:37,720 --> 00:02:39,240
Don't single me out or anything.

53
00:02:39,700 --> 00:02:43,380
I hand-selected you girls to come back to life and bring Saga to life, too!

54
00:02:43,600 --> 00:02:44,680
You can accomplish anything!

55
00:02:44,680 --> 00:02:48,640
So on March 8th, EFS will be jam-packed with your fans!

56
00:02:49,160 --> 00:02:52,660
I say, get the crowd all fired up and encore with that new number!

57
00:02:53,020 --> 00:02:53,420
Yeah!

58
00:02:56,300 --> 00:02:58,160
This bomb is still lit!

59
00:02:58,460 --> 00:03:00,640
Soon everyone will know Frans Choushu!

60
00:03:03,740 --> 00:03:08,740
Shades is always drinking the dumbass juice, but even I can tell he chugged the whole bottle this time.

61
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:10,180
Is this really gonna work?

62
00:03:10,360 --> 00:03:12,140
Normally, I'd say it's impossible.

63
00:03:12,560 --> 00:03:14,180
You're right, it's just not realistic.

64
00:03:14,180 --> 00:03:15,140
Yeah, but...

65
00:03:15,140 --> 00:03:15,740
Yeah, but...

66
00:03:15,740 --> 00:03:16,360
I know.

67
00:03:16,640 --> 00:03:18,760
We're long past considering what's realistic.

68
00:03:19,400 --> 00:03:20,160
Good point.

69
00:03:20,440 --> 00:03:26,200
If Mr. Kotaro's really this dead set on it, maybe he's got a good reason we don't know about yet.

70
00:03:26,420 --> 00:03:28,220
Doesn't he just pull stuff out of his butt?

71
00:03:28,220 --> 00:03:34,560
I say... we try.

72
00:03:34,560 --> 00:03:35,360
Huh?

73
00:03:35,360 --> 00:03:37,900
Do you realize what a big risk this is?

74
00:03:37,900 --> 00:03:39,460
I don't know if we'll be successful.

75
00:03:39,460 --> 00:03:44,340
But if it's a chance for all of us to sing and dance together, then I'm more than up for it.

76
00:03:44,340 --> 00:03:47,720
What matters to me is performing with you guys.

77
00:03:47,720 --> 00:03:50,020
You're on.

78
00:03:50,020 --> 00:03:52,480
You're right, the show Arpino is terrible.

79
00:03:52,480 --> 00:03:54,040
And we made it through that.

80
00:03:54,040 --> 00:03:57,000
Besides, everything that we do is bold and brazen.

81
00:03:57,000 --> 00:03:59,200
Yeah, I mean, we're already zombies.

82
00:03:59,940 --> 00:04:02,320
So it's not like this is gonna kill us, am I right?

83
00:04:02,380 --> 00:04:06,740
Just listening to each of you talk makes me feel like we can actually do this.

84
00:04:07,060 --> 00:04:08,080
I'm kind of shocked.

85
00:04:08,080 --> 00:04:13,100
What am I gonna do with you crazies?

86
00:04:13,840 --> 00:04:17,540
For this to work out, we need the show to be even better than Arpino.

87
00:04:17,540 --> 00:04:20,720
If we do anything less than our best, then we're certain to fail.

88
00:04:21,020 --> 00:04:23,080
Okay, now whip us into shape, I.

89
00:04:23,440 --> 00:04:24,320
No problem.

90
00:04:24,600 --> 00:04:27,360
Time to address everything I've been letting you guys slide on.

91
00:04:27,500 --> 00:04:27,840
Mm-hmm.

92
00:04:28,260 --> 00:04:29,160
Mostly you.

93
00:04:29,340 --> 00:04:31,520
Uh, come on, don't be too mean.

94
00:04:31,820 --> 00:04:32,380
What's wrong?

95
00:04:32,460 --> 00:04:33,340
You can't handle it.

96
00:04:34,400 --> 00:04:34,580
Ha!

97
00:04:38,080 --> 00:04:44,640
Looks like there's still something bugging you.

98
00:04:45,020 --> 00:04:46,620
Well, how could this not bug me?

99
00:04:47,240 --> 00:04:48,980
It is where I died, after all.

100
00:04:49,320 --> 00:04:50,520
You can't die twice.

101
00:04:50,700 --> 00:04:51,960
No point in being scared.

102
00:04:51,960 --> 00:04:55,660
I don't think you're the one to talk to since you jumped off the same cliff twice.

103
00:04:59,380 --> 00:05:00,100
Hey, Ai.

104
00:05:00,560 --> 00:05:02,400
Remember what you said back at the park?

105
00:05:02,900 --> 00:05:04,600
I don't care if I'm a zombie.

106
00:05:05,020 --> 00:05:06,900
I'm gonna get back on stage again.

107
00:05:06,900 --> 00:05:08,680
And then I'll...

108
00:05:08,680 --> 00:05:10,080
Let's make it happen.

109
00:05:10,580 --> 00:05:12,940
If something goes wrong, I'll take care of it for us.

110
00:05:13,400 --> 00:05:16,200
I'm the boss, and the boss can't be afraid to get her hands dirty.

111
00:05:16,760 --> 00:05:17,920
Leader, not boss.

112
00:05:18,060 --> 00:05:18,840
Same thing.

113
00:05:19,620 --> 00:05:20,060
Huh?

114
00:05:20,580 --> 00:05:21,720
Damn, that's scary!

115
00:05:22,140 --> 00:05:24,320
I wanted to make sure you guys were okay.

116
00:05:24,860 --> 00:05:25,680
Um, yeah.

117
00:05:25,940 --> 00:05:27,560
It wasn't anything serious, sir.

118
00:05:27,560 --> 00:05:28,220
We'll be fine.

119
00:05:28,220 --> 00:05:30,520
I'll be there to back you up, too.

120
00:05:31,280 --> 00:05:33,840
And I'm sorry for eavesdropping, but I couldn't help it.

121
00:05:34,240 --> 00:05:34,740
I know!

122
00:05:34,940 --> 00:05:36,820
We should have a rally to build up our morale!

123
00:05:37,380 --> 00:05:39,240
We're idols, not bikers, Saki.

124
00:05:39,240 --> 00:05:50,820
No, that isn't it.

125
00:05:52,400 --> 00:05:54,140
There's no way we'll pull it off!

126
00:05:57,640 --> 00:05:59,340
La, la, la, loo, la, loo, la...

127
00:05:59,340 --> 00:06:00,300
That doesn't work.

128
00:06:04,020 --> 00:06:05,900
This place is huge.

129
00:06:05,900 --> 00:06:07,740
Question.

130
00:06:08,140 --> 00:06:08,380
Hmm.

131
00:06:08,660 --> 00:06:11,720
I was too nervous to ask before, but...

132
00:06:11,720 --> 00:06:14,520
Would you mind telling me how many tickets we've sold so far?

133
00:06:14,800 --> 00:06:15,820
I didn't print any.

134
00:06:16,320 --> 00:06:16,760
Huh?

135
00:06:17,240 --> 00:06:18,280
What did you say?

136
00:06:18,500 --> 00:06:20,080
We're only selling them day of.

137
00:06:20,520 --> 00:06:22,140
But why would you do that?

138
00:06:22,240 --> 00:06:26,600
With this concert, we need to put out the message that Franshushu has risen in Saga.

139
00:06:27,060 --> 00:06:30,400
That means it should be legendary in as many ways as possible.

140
00:06:30,920 --> 00:06:32,440
Ordinary methods won't cut it.

141
00:06:32,440 --> 00:06:36,200
Remember everything you've accomplished so far.

142
00:06:37,200 --> 00:06:40,600
Believe in Franshushu, and believe in me as well.

143
00:06:50,180 --> 00:06:51,640
Oh my gosh.

144
00:06:51,780 --> 00:06:54,140
The whole crowd fits in the VIP area.

145
00:06:54,140 --> 00:06:56,700
Um, hey guys.

146
00:06:57,160 --> 00:06:57,920
Glad you're here.

147
00:06:58,420 --> 00:07:02,200
We are, uh, Franshushu.

148
00:07:02,200 --> 00:07:02,420
Come on.

149
00:07:23,500 --> 00:07:24,500
Oh my gosh.

150
00:07:24,500 --> 00:07:34,880
Should we yell for an encore?

151
00:07:35,300 --> 00:07:36,180
No way, Chul.

152
00:07:36,800 --> 00:07:37,680
Better be cruel.

153
00:07:38,900 --> 00:07:40,520
Could this be the end?

154
00:07:54,500 --> 00:08:12,480
Ladies, I'm home!

155
00:08:12,480 --> 00:08:17,300
Oh look, if it isn't the legendary Fryster Pooh!

156
00:08:17,440 --> 00:08:18,980
Mr. Kotaro, where were you?

157
00:08:19,160 --> 00:08:20,220
We've been worried sick!

158
00:08:20,240 --> 00:08:21,740
Don't you worry, baby Zed.

159
00:08:21,740 --> 00:08:24,820
You know, your trusty old commander won't go MIA forever?

160
00:08:27,640 --> 00:08:29,500
Don't tell me you were drinking all night.

161
00:08:29,620 --> 00:08:30,420
Yeah, obviously.

162
00:08:30,800 --> 00:08:31,760
Because guess what, girls?

163
00:08:31,840 --> 00:08:35,340
We are drowning in debt now for about 20 mil.

164
00:08:36,620 --> 00:08:37,680
Crazy, ain't it?

165
00:08:37,780 --> 00:08:38,700
Yes, sirree.

166
00:08:38,880 --> 00:08:40,940
We are 20 million dee.

167
00:08:41,140 --> 00:08:41,900
We're in debt?

168
00:08:42,560 --> 00:08:43,860
No, that can't be right.

169
00:08:44,100 --> 00:08:44,700
No way.

170
00:08:45,240 --> 00:08:46,200
I mean, yeah.

171
00:08:46,520 --> 00:08:49,680
That was a large-scale concert and it failed tremendously.

172
00:08:49,680 --> 00:08:51,260
Of course we're in debt.

173
00:08:51,740 --> 00:08:52,860
Relax!

174
00:08:53,400 --> 00:08:54,860
No use of crying now!

175
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:56,200
Front Shoo Shoo's done for!

176
00:08:56,400 --> 00:08:57,740
Saga's done for too!

177
00:08:57,880 --> 00:08:58,980
It's all done!

178
00:08:59,220 --> 00:09:00,860
Let's pack it in, everybody!

179
00:09:02,800 --> 00:09:06,000
Shades has been on his little bender for two whole weeks now.

180
00:09:06,680 --> 00:09:09,320
And our food supply's been depleted for seven days.

181
00:09:09,900 --> 00:09:13,040
Yeah, but zombies don't need to eat, so it's not that big of an issue, right?

182
00:09:13,360 --> 00:09:14,020
Who knows?

183
00:09:14,100 --> 00:09:17,020
Maybe he's coming up with an amazing plan to fix all this right now.

184
00:09:17,180 --> 00:09:18,360
He's done it before, remember?

185
00:09:19,000 --> 00:09:20,980
That asshat doesn't plan for crap!

186
00:09:21,180 --> 00:09:23,060
That's how we ended up in this whole mess!

187
00:09:23,420 --> 00:09:25,340
Hey, don't take your feelings out on Sakura.

188
00:09:25,600 --> 00:09:27,680
You're not the only one who's irritated, you know.

189
00:09:28,000 --> 00:09:29,320
Then I'll take him out on you!

190
00:09:29,700 --> 00:09:30,940
Please don't fight, you two.

191
00:09:31,080 --> 00:09:33,080
It's times like this we need to stick together.

192
00:09:33,340 --> 00:09:36,040
We'll be okay somehow, even if he gives up on us.

193
00:09:36,040 --> 00:09:40,020
You say that, but without Mr. Tatsumi's help, we can't do our makeup.

194
00:09:40,280 --> 00:09:42,400
Which means we can't go shopping or anything either.

195
00:09:42,900 --> 00:09:45,660
And the longer this goes on, the bigger our debt is going to get.

196
00:09:46,040 --> 00:09:50,620
I'm sorry, Sakura, but it'll take a lot more than positivity to take care of this problem.

197
00:09:57,280 --> 00:09:57,760
Tai?

198
00:09:58,660 --> 00:10:00,600
Damn, your face looks busted.

199
00:10:06,040 --> 00:10:17,240
She got that by herself?

200
00:10:17,500 --> 00:10:18,600
I guess.

201
00:10:18,760 --> 00:10:20,340
Which means she swiped his cash?

202
00:10:20,420 --> 00:10:21,720
And painted her face?

203
00:10:21,740 --> 00:10:21,980
Mm-hmm.

204
00:10:22,960 --> 00:10:24,140
That's crazy.

205
00:10:27,720 --> 00:10:28,940
This proves it.

206
00:10:29,180 --> 00:10:30,180
We were wrong.

207
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:34,140
We can do anything if we try, just like Tai did.

208
00:10:34,140 --> 00:10:37,340
The problem is, we haven't been trying our best.

209
00:10:37,780 --> 00:10:40,020
We're so used to him calling the shots.

210
00:10:40,760 --> 00:10:43,320
And with him gone, we assumed that we had to give up.

211
00:10:43,440 --> 00:10:43,740
Yeah.

212
00:10:44,260 --> 00:10:47,540
At some point, we started relying on him too much and took him for granted.

213
00:10:47,980 --> 00:10:48,380
Right.

214
00:10:48,600 --> 00:10:50,440
That's what happened with the EFS show.

215
00:10:50,960 --> 00:10:54,900
All we thought was that if we do our best, he'll make everything else come together.

216
00:10:55,840 --> 00:10:57,380
And clearly, that's not true.

217
00:10:59,380 --> 00:11:02,280
Since we've got the makeup, guess we might as well use it.

218
00:11:02,280 --> 00:11:04,580
Sounds fun, but how do we pay out the debt?

219
00:11:04,960 --> 00:11:05,660
By working.

220
00:11:05,860 --> 00:11:10,220
If we can't do idle stuff right now, then let's try to get part-time jobs until it's possible.

221
00:11:10,620 --> 00:11:11,000
Cool.

222
00:11:11,120 --> 00:11:12,200
Can I help out too?

223
00:11:12,580 --> 00:11:13,060
Sure.

224
00:11:13,280 --> 00:11:14,080
Let's do it.

225
00:11:14,320 --> 00:11:14,640
Yeah.

226
00:11:14,820 --> 00:11:15,960
We're good under pressure.

227
00:11:16,620 --> 00:11:18,540
Time for us to do the thinking ourselves.

228
00:11:18,760 --> 00:11:21,740
We can move forward without letting the past bring us down.

229
00:11:21,740 --> 00:11:27,180
That's right.

230
00:11:27,460 --> 00:11:29,180
In the end, I still happened.

231
00:11:30,800 --> 00:11:31,620
What's up?

232
00:11:32,520 --> 00:11:33,260
I'm in.

233
00:11:34,040 --> 00:11:36,860
We may be zombies, but there's still life in us.

234
00:11:37,280 --> 00:11:38,160
You're right.

235
00:11:38,520 --> 00:11:40,940
Let's work hard so we can get our revenge.

236
00:11:40,940 --> 00:11:56,440
That's a shame.

237
00:11:56,760 --> 00:11:57,660
He's dead as dirt.

238
00:11:58,160 --> 00:11:59,060
What's all that?

239
00:11:59,260 --> 00:12:00,400
Just a bunch of squid?

240
00:12:00,660 --> 00:12:01,400
Looks that way.

241
00:12:01,660 --> 00:12:02,840
I'm not sure why, though.

242
00:12:03,020 --> 00:12:04,020
He coughed!

243
00:12:04,080 --> 00:12:05,120
Oh, he's alive!

244
00:12:05,120 --> 00:12:05,880
You all right?

245
00:12:05,880 --> 00:12:10,900
I'm better than ever.

246
00:12:11,200 --> 00:12:12,960
Just got a little swept away is all.

247
00:12:18,000 --> 00:12:19,840
And then the guy walked off!

248
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:21,600
Dude, how crazy is that?

249
00:12:21,760 --> 00:12:23,840
We got ourselves a mysterious squid man.

250
00:12:24,400 --> 00:12:25,860
I'll let you take that one.

251
00:12:26,060 --> 00:12:26,320
What?

252
00:12:26,940 --> 00:12:29,060
Well, your story must be pretty important, then.

253
00:12:29,580 --> 00:12:32,500
I think even the Tokyo pubs are going to want this.

254
00:12:32,780 --> 00:12:33,340
Oh, really?

255
00:12:33,600 --> 00:12:34,160
Clock's ticking.

256
00:12:34,460 --> 00:12:34,740
Right.

257
00:12:34,960 --> 00:12:35,260
Gotcha.

258
00:12:35,880 --> 00:12:38,660
Later, then, I got myself a squid man to track down.

259
00:12:46,460 --> 00:12:47,340
Morning, ladies.

260
00:12:47,720 --> 00:12:49,040
What happened to you?

261
00:12:49,360 --> 00:12:49,840
Irrelevant.

262
00:12:54,460 --> 00:12:55,260
Aren't you gonna—

263
00:12:55,260 --> 00:12:58,280
One year ago, I made a big mistake.

264
00:12:58,280 --> 00:13:04,000
On the last 8th of March, at my behest, you performed in a show that failed enormously.

265
00:13:04,000 --> 00:13:05,000
I'm sorry.

266
00:13:05,000 --> 00:13:05,480
I'm sorry.

267
00:13:08,620 --> 00:13:11,660
That's why next month, you will return to EFS.

268
00:13:11,660 --> 00:13:13,960
Your revenge show is March 8th.

269
00:13:17,960 --> 00:13:19,960
Your revenge show is March 8th.

270
00:13:19,960 --> 00:13:20,320
Hey!

271
00:13:20,320 --> 00:13:22,940
That said, the approach will be different.

272
00:13:22,940 --> 00:13:24,940
I'm not just banking on our momentum.

273
00:13:24,940 --> 00:13:29,480
This year, you've breathed new life into Franz Shushu.

274
00:13:29,480 --> 00:13:36,100
Your album and merch sales have been plentiful, like the rice in the fields of Hanamura and Warabino.

275
00:13:36,100 --> 00:13:40,000
More importantly, the seven of you have truly grown.

276
00:13:40,000 --> 00:13:44,160
But despite all that, this show won't be easy.

277
00:13:44,160 --> 00:13:48,840
Right now, I'm working on a variety of advertising projects to build up some hype.

278
00:13:48,840 --> 00:13:52,260
I promise you girls, I'm giving this all I have.

279
00:13:52,260 --> 00:13:59,260
Someday, when Franz Shushu is an even greater known legend, that failure will be a brief chapter in our tale.

280
00:13:59,260 --> 00:14:02,260
That's why you picked March 8th.

281
00:14:02,260 --> 00:14:03,260
Listen!

282
00:14:03,260 --> 00:14:05,260
This battle will be fierce.

283
00:14:05,260 --> 00:14:06,260
But take heart!

284
00:14:06,260 --> 00:14:10,260
Because of your heroic act, Saga will be forever changed!

285
00:14:10,260 --> 00:14:16,260
Even if Saga itself is plunged into darkness and despair, the seven of you will still remain!

286
00:14:16,260 --> 00:14:22,260
A bright light, shining eternally throughout that pit of oblivion!

287
00:14:22,260 --> 00:14:23,260
Never forget!

288
00:14:23,260 --> 00:14:28,260
I hand-selected each of you to come back from the dead to become the new heroes of Saga!

289
00:14:28,260 --> 00:14:37,260
And when your revenge is set into motion, that's the signal for Saga's counterattack to begin!

290
00:14:40,260 --> 00:14:41,260
What's with the sneeze?

291
00:14:41,260 --> 00:14:42,260
A little cold.

292
00:14:42,260 --> 00:14:43,260
I thought it was cute.

293
00:14:43,260 --> 00:14:45,260
That killed the whole thing!

294
00:14:45,260 --> 00:14:46,260
Oh!

295
00:14:46,260 --> 00:14:47,260
Shut up!

296
00:14:54,260 --> 00:14:56,260
Kotaro Tatsumi, isn't it?

297
00:14:58,260 --> 00:15:00,260
I'm Arata Okuba.

298
00:15:00,260 --> 00:15:02,260
I write for Saga Zine.

299
00:15:02,260 --> 00:15:03,260
Yeah.

300
00:15:03,260 --> 00:15:05,260
I read your articles pretty often.

301
00:15:05,260 --> 00:15:08,260
It's a shame what happened a year ago.

302
00:15:08,260 --> 00:15:12,260
But it seems like your girls have been really outdoing themselves recently.

303
00:15:12,260 --> 00:15:15,260
Are you here to reflect on past mistakes?

304
00:15:15,260 --> 00:15:16,260
Sorry.

305
00:15:16,260 --> 00:15:18,260
I'm not doing personal interviews.

306
00:15:18,260 --> 00:15:22,260
You stay in my line of work long enough and you end up with acquaintances all over the place.

307
00:15:23,260 --> 00:15:26,260
That said, it took me a while to connect the dots this time.

308
00:15:26,260 --> 00:15:37,260
Sakura Minamoto, Saki Nikaido, Ai Mizuno, Miss Junko Kono, Lily Hoshikawa slash Masao Go, and Tai Yamada.

309
00:15:37,260 --> 00:15:40,260
All of those people are dead.

310
00:15:40,260 --> 00:15:45,260
Sadly, I wasn't able to dig up any until about number five.

311
00:15:45,260 --> 00:15:46,260
Heh.

312
00:15:46,260 --> 00:15:48,260
You ready to talk?

313
00:15:48,260 --> 00:15:50,260
What exactly are these women?

314
00:15:51,260 --> 00:15:53,260
These pictures beg a lot of questions.

315
00:15:55,260 --> 00:15:57,260
I can have their graves exhumed, you know.

316
00:15:58,260 --> 00:16:00,260
Why write something like this?

317
00:16:00,260 --> 00:16:07,260
Because I feel compelled to stop you from trying to profit off these poor deceased girls by turning them into singing and dancing clowns.

318
00:16:07,260 --> 00:16:09,260
Is that reason enough for you?

319
00:16:09,260 --> 00:16:12,260
Feel free to stay silent.

320
00:16:12,260 --> 00:16:15,260
But after the article is published, your big secret will be out.

321
00:16:16,260 --> 00:16:17,260
It's shocking news.

322
00:16:18,260 --> 00:16:19,260
I wonder what the public will think.

323
00:16:21,260 --> 00:16:24,260
They'll be here next month, performing in a big concert.

324
00:16:25,260 --> 00:16:26,260
What?

325
00:16:26,260 --> 00:16:27,260
It's their revenge.

326
00:16:27,260 --> 00:16:28,260
You're insane.

327
00:16:28,260 --> 00:16:30,260
Why would you want to recreate such a disaster?

328
00:16:30,260 --> 00:16:33,260
How dare you turn the dead into cheap entertainment?

329
00:16:34,260 --> 00:16:38,260
You can publish anything you like, but you'll never stop Franshu Shuu.

330
00:16:39,260 --> 00:16:44,260
I'll make sure they don't take that stage.

331
00:16:55,260 --> 00:16:56,260
You okay down there?

332
00:17:01,260 --> 00:17:05,260
The high school girl kept her mouth shut, but I doubt it'll work out that way this time.

333
00:17:05,260 --> 00:17:09,260
Though if I'm being honest, I was a little surprised that the word didn't get out sooner.

334
00:17:10,260 --> 00:17:12,260
And the reporter's not your only problem.

335
00:17:13,260 --> 00:17:17,260
Things have been rough lately, but this'll be worse than some scratches and stolen clothes.

336
00:17:18,260 --> 00:17:19,260
I don't care about that crap.

337
00:17:20,260 --> 00:17:22,260
This show is gonna be a roaring success.

338
00:17:23,260 --> 00:17:24,260
I won't screw up again.

339
00:17:25,260 --> 00:17:31,260
Hm. Twelve years ago, when I first ran into that gloomy half-crazed kid, I never thought he could make all of this happen.

340
00:17:31,260 --> 00:17:36,260
If I wasn't gloomy and half-crazed, then I doubt I would have believed you.

341
00:17:37,260 --> 00:17:41,260
That you're immortal, fighting a curse that's been at work in Saga for centuries.

342
00:17:42,260 --> 00:17:44,260
And that part about how you can revive the dead.

343
00:17:44,260 --> 00:17:46,260
Hm. But you got what you wanted.

344
00:17:47,260 --> 00:17:48,260
Not yet.

345
00:17:49,260 --> 00:17:52,260
I still have to find a way to stop your prophecy from coming true.

346
00:17:53,260 --> 00:17:57,260
As the Rewa era starts, Saga will face a cataclysmic threat.

347
00:17:58,260 --> 00:18:01,260
A powerful phenomenon will cause thoughts of Saga to disappear,

348
00:18:01,260 --> 00:18:04,260
and even memories of Saga's past will be lost forever.

349
00:18:05,260 --> 00:18:08,260
Of course, things were already looking dire enough with the population decreasing.

350
00:18:09,260 --> 00:18:13,260
Exactly. So the obvious solution was to create something in Saga that's impossible to forget.

351
00:18:13,260 --> 00:18:18,260
Gathering young women killed by the curse who otherwise would have brought glory to this region,

352
00:18:19,260 --> 00:18:22,260
and making them into a popular idol group that the people of Saga can be proud of?

353
00:18:23,260 --> 00:18:27,260
I admit, it's a great idea, this Mount Mifuneyama Rakuin project of yours.

354
00:18:28,260 --> 00:18:30,260
It's called the Zombieland Saga Project.

355
00:18:31,260 --> 00:18:32,260
That's what I meant.

356
00:18:33,260 --> 00:18:36,260
The world is shaped by the actions of men.

357
00:18:36,260 --> 00:18:38,260
You're wrong there.

358
00:18:39,260 --> 00:18:40,260
Men and zombies.

359
00:18:41,260 --> 00:18:43,260
It's both, hand in hand.

360
00:18:47,260 --> 00:18:51,260
All of Kyushu is under a severe rain warning tonight and into tomorrow morning.

361
00:18:54,260 --> 00:18:55,260
That's a lot of rain.

362
00:18:56,260 --> 00:18:57,260
I wonder if Kokoro's okay?

363
00:18:58,260 --> 00:18:59,260
He'll be fine.

364
00:19:00,260 --> 00:19:01,260
I sure hope so.

365
00:19:01,260 --> 00:19:03,260
When he gets back, we ought to blast him with the waterproof spray.

366
00:19:03,260 --> 00:19:06,260
Tomorrow's when our badass revenge officially starts.

367
00:19:07,260 --> 00:19:08,260
We should probably get some rest.

368
00:19:09,260 --> 00:19:10,260
Yeah.

369
00:19:16,260 --> 00:19:17,260
Kay, done.

370
00:19:18,260 --> 00:19:20,260
This sure has been a hell of an article to write.

371
00:19:22,260 --> 00:19:24,260
Next month, they'll be doing a concert here.

372
00:19:26,260 --> 00:19:29,260
You can't dishonor the dead like that, I'll show him!

373
00:19:30,260 --> 00:19:31,260
What the hell?

374
00:19:32,260 --> 00:19:33,260
Are you kidding me?

375
00:19:34,260 --> 00:19:35,260
Mm-hmm.

376
00:19:36,260 --> 00:19:37,260
This is it.

377
00:19:38,260 --> 00:19:39,260
Get ready!

